{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf","id":409279,"title":"Mage Transitioning to Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-17T13:45:31-08:00","id":409279,"title":"Mage Transitioning to Werewolf","content":"I know its not possible for other main splats to stack up (hybrids, no thank you). But what about changing that character's splat to another? So I was reading &quot;Equinox Road&quot; from Changeling about Mages transitioning into Changelings due to the hedge's power. Now it got me thinking... Well...Mages are humans with magical powers. But I remembered that their awakened souls protects them from changing into another creature. But what about the 2ed rules for Wolf-Bloods? I checked and not much information, duh. So what do you guys think? Is it possible for a Mage to transition into a Werewolf? Losing it's magic/awakened powers and becoming one of the Uratha. If its possible, then boy do I have a game scratching up in my head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:05:24-08:00","id":409308,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why you couldn't make it so even if it isn't. But werewolf splat does override anything human, so psychics lose their abilities when they go uratha. Not that you couldn't fudge that up either. <br /> <br /> You could have a Mage get bit by a dire formed uratha, have him botch a lunacy roll and turn wolf blooded and go from there though! Keeps it all Hollywood horror too as theres a wolf blooded tell that has them shift dire in kuruth. All american werewolf in London style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:16:24-08:00","id":409322,"title":"","content":"Ha ha I was thinking the same thing! Classic Hollywood werewolf, never gets old. Anyways, if it becomes an official rule, then awesome! It would make Mage and Werewolf crossovers even more interesting. Though my curiosity is getting the best of me about First Change or Final Change, and how do they gain it now? Can it automatically happen without being a Wolf-Blood? Gosh I really can't wait to get my hands on the 2ed book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T23:55:44-08:00","id":409759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf#post409279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know its not possible for other main splats to stack up (hybrids, no thank you). But what about changing that character's splat to another? So I was reading &quot;Equinox Road&quot; from Changeling about Mages transitioning into Changelings due to the hedge's power. Now it got me thinking... Well...Mages are humans with magical powers. But I remembered that their awakened souls protects them from changing into another creature. But what about the 2ed rules for Wolf-Bloods? I checked and not much information, duh. So what do you guys think? Is it possible for a Mage to transition into a Werewolf? Losing it's magic/awakened powers and becoming one of the Uratha. If its possible, then boy do I have a game scratching up in my head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That Changeling thing is a bit of a debate(I assume you're talking about the Unmade?), but...<br /> <br /> 1) From the outside perspective, nothing can force a trade of a template. A mage will just die in the Hedge or in the arms of a Stranger as much as when Embraced. It's one of those few concepts held up a lot<br /> <br /> 2) From the inside perspective, a mage can't become a changeling (or a 'changeling') until they cannibalize their own souls enough for the Arcadian powers to deal with them, and even then it's implied that only Dusk will make deals with them at that point. It's...not a happy affair.<br /> <br /> As for a mage becoming a werewolf...Well, probably not possible unless you just decides it happens. Signing a Watchertower is a strong enough expression of individuality that it actually kind of warps and 'cleanses' the body of pre-existing conditions like Uratha Genetics. When you join with the Supernal, you declare the right of humanity, to be self-deterministic, and reject any claims of Moon or blood of Wolf as having a hold on you. You can make those choices after the fact, but when a Wolf-Blooded Awakens, they choose, at the least, to move beyond becoming one of the People.<br /> <br /> Now of course, this all flies out the window if you decide it, and certainly precedence exists for prior claims taking over. Matt McFarland said he heartily approved of Demon-Blooded retaining their Cipher(and maybe more) upon Awakening, and I don't see a reason why a Mage couldn't be wolf-blooded. Not much of a further step to say that the Moon can yank the chains out.<br /> <br /> But canonically, Awakening precludes becoming an Uratha like it does becoming a Changeling. In order to allow it after the fact, the idea is that something drastic has to happen in exchange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T23:59:41-08:00","id":409762,"title":"","content":"Isn't the whole thing about Mages and Arcadia is that the Thorns strip away the Awakened soul? I distinctly remember something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:07:32-08:00","id":409766,"title":"","content":"I might need to poke into Equinox Road, because on the one hand , it does, but on the other hand Awakened souls are resilient fuckers. A mage is likely to go insane before losing their soul.<br /> <br /> But I might be wrong. Equinox Road/Rites of Spring AWAY!<br /> <br /> EDIT; A quick check confirms it, unless someone taking time finds something else. Mage's suffer the thorns like mortals do, but that says nothing about it killing a mage's soul. The only mention of something resembling mechanics for that is the Unmade, and again, that's...not a sane way of going about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-18-2015, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:49:59-08:00","id":409777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409759#post409759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As for a mage becoming a werewolf...Well, probably not possible unless you just decides it happens. Signing a Watchertower is a strong enough expression of individuality that it actually kind of warps and 'cleanses' the body of pre-existing conditions like Uratha Genetics. When you join with the Supernal, you declare the right of humanity, to be self-deterministic, and reject any claims of Moon or blood of Wolf as having a hold on you. You can make those choices after the fact, but when a Wolf-Blooded Awakens, they choose, at the least, to move beyond becoming one of the People.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Awakening knocks Supernatural Merits off (and in 2e converts them into Arcane Experiences), and &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; in Forsaken 2e means any one of a wide range of things, most or all of which are Supernatural Merits. So if you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone who turns Dalu in the full moon,&quot; they'd lose it upon Awakening, but they <i>can</i> still Awaken. If you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone genetically related to a Werewolf,&quot; then sure they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages can even join Packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:54:54-08:00","id":409780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409777#post409777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Awakening knocks Supernatural Merits off (and in 2e converts them into Arcane Experiences), and &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; in Forsaken 2e means any one of a wide range of things, most or all of which are Supernatural Merits. So if you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone who turns Dalu in the full moon,&quot; they'd lose it upon Awakening, but they <i>can</i> still Awaken. If you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone genetically related to a Werewolf,&quot; then sure they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages can even join Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Underneath Arcane speaking out of his ass, this is what he meant to say, yes.<br /> <br /> One day I'll remember to stop the crazy talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-18-2015, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T01:02:07-08:00","id":409782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409777#post409777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Awakening knocks Supernatural Merits off (and in 2e converts them into Arcane Experiences), and &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; in Forsaken 2e means any one of a wide range of things, most or all of which are Supernatural Merits. So if you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone who turns Dalu in the full moon,&quot; they'd lose it upon Awakening, but they <i>can</i> still Awaken. If you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone genetically related to a Werewolf,&quot; then sure they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages can even join Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does raise the question, though: Could a wolf-blooded Mage's children become werewolves? How about that for a screwed-up family!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:51:56-08:00","id":410136,"title":"","content":"Thought as much. But what about a Mage becoming a full fledge Uratha? Losing it's magic and such. *Sigh* I guess I'm throwing my curiosity out too early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:38:27-08:00","id":410542,"title":"","content":"Not in the games as written, no - once you have a Power Stat, you're locked into it forever (bar things like Promethean New Dawn). Mages can't become Werewolves, and Werewolves can't Awaken.<br /> <br /> In your game? Go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:11:19-08:00","id":410583,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. I guess I thought of Mages as human as Hunters, that's why. Sure, in personal games I probably would allow it, makes things more dramatic and interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:16:25-08:00","id":410588,"title":"","content":"Add the bite too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:20:58-08:00","id":410590,"title":"","content":"Technically it can be done.<br /> <br /> There's a Numina Angels and some spirits can use that resurrects the dead. They have their template erased in the process, allowing them to become any other template. So if a Mage bound one of those angels or spirits and went on a mage killing spree, they could force the angel to resurrect them, allowing them to one day be werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T15:31:27-08:00","id":410646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=410588#post410588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add the bite too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yeah! Reminds me when Constantine became a werewolf himself, totally loved it! If I can find the picture...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:33:22-08:00","id":410726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409777#post409777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Awakening knocks Supernatural Merits off (and in 2e converts them into Arcane Experiences), and &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; in Forsaken 2e means any one of a wide range of things, most or all of which are Supernatural Merits. So if you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone who turns Dalu in the full moon,&quot; they'd lose it upon Awakening, but they <i>can</i> still Awaken. If you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone genetically related to a Werewolf,&quot; then sure they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages can even join Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave's actually <i>slightly </i>wrong here - the Wolf-Blooded thing of 'turns into Dalu under full moon / other supernatural tell' isn't actually a Merit (at least as of the 2nd draft of Idigam), but it does have some supernatural merits that you can then bolt onto it.<br /> <br /> Given the way that Tells work, it wouldn't be <i>terribly</i> troublesome to have an Awakened Wolf-Blooded keep their Tell, but you're probably best off just assuming that the Awakening clears off the full Wolf-Blooded package, Tells and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:21:28-08:00","id":410871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409777#post409777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can even join Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>WaitwaitwaitwaitWHAT?<br /> <br /> <br /> That's awesome. I take it that it's also possible for Vampires to do the same? I'd really love seeing a Gangrel or two running with the werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:29:19-08:00","id":410880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=410726#post410726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dave's actually <i>slightly </i>wrong here - the Wolf-Blooded thing of 'turns into Dalu under full moon / other supernatural tell' isn't actually a Merit (at least as of the 2nd draft of Idigam), but it does have some supernatural merits that you can then bolt onto it.<br /> <br /> Given the way that Tells work, it wouldn't be <i>terribly</i> troublesome to have an Awakened Wolf-Blooded keep their Tell, but you're probably best off just assuming that the Awakening clears off the full Wolf-Blooded package, Tells and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa! So its possible for a wolf-blooded Mage? Nice...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:32:26-08:00","id":410883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=410871#post410871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WaitwaitwaitwaitWHAT?<br /> <br /> <br /> That's awesome. I take it that it's also possible for Vampires to do the same? I'd really love seeing a Gangrel or two running with the werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be nice if vampires could, if only for this sitcom I'm building with a friend of mine where two vampires and a werewolf share a flat in London (Soho, to be specific).<br /> <br /> Or the elegant Ventrue elder in Tokyo who got seduced by a werewolf until they started running with their pack and abandoned politics and society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:47:37-08:00","id":410893,"title":"","content":"In my vampire game one of the characters became chummy with the werewolves, it might have been appropriate to bring her in after the things she set up for them.<br /> <br /> If mages can it doesn't seem like vampires or anything else would be unable to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T20:29:54-08:00","id":410966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409777#post409777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Awakening knocks Supernatural Merits off (and in 2e converts them into Arcane Experiences), and &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; in Forsaken 2e means any one of a wide range of things, most or all of which are Supernatural Merits. So if you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone who turns Dalu in the full moon,&quot; they'd lose it upon Awakening, but they <i>can</i> still Awaken. If you mean &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; as &quot;someone genetically related to a Werewolf,&quot; then sure they can Awaken.<br /> <br /> Mages can even join Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick question that is only partially related to this topic, Dave, but will Sleepwalkers be a series of merits like Ghouls and Wolf Blooded in the 2nd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:53:29-08:00","id":411111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=409782#post409782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This does raise the question, though: Could a wolf-blooded Mage's children become werewolves? How about that for a screwed-up family!</div> </div> </div> </div>Any human *could* become a werewolf. Sometimes Luna's fickle that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:02:44-08:00","id":411117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=411111#post411111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any human *could* become a werewolf. Sometimes Luna's fickle that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could an Archmaster block Luna from making their children Werewolves without violating the Pax? Would Luna making an Archmage's (or anyone's, I suppose) children into Werewolves specifically to <i>stop</i> that person Awakening be a violation of the Pax? Would Luna even <i>care</i> about the Pax?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:51:52-08:00","id":411140,"title":"","content":"YMMV*<br /> <br /> Translation: I doubt these would ever get hard answers. Do what works for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T03:56:21-08:00","id":411270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=410871#post410871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WaitwaitwaitwaitWHAT?<br /> <br /> That's awesome. I take it that it's also possible for Vampires to do the same? I'd really love seeing a Gangrel or two running with the werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno whether vampires can, can't remember if there's any limitation based on having to be alive or whatnot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My own tendency would be to allow it; it certainly gets entertaining when you start bringing vampires in as the targets of some pack rites <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=411117#post411117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could an Archmaster block Luna from making their children Werewolves without violating the Pax? Would Luna making an Archmage's (or anyone's, I suppose) children into Werewolves specifically to <i>stop</i> that person Awakening be a violation of the Pax? Would Luna even <i>care</i> about the Pax?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Bunyip says, I suspect this will not be particularly detailed, or at least the answers in a Mage book that covered it would be different to the answers in a Werewolf book that did so.<br /> <br /> My <i>personal</i> take on it - and note that I bend, twist and fold the Awakening setting to fit my Werewolf games as I see fit - would be:<br /> - An Archmaster could try to block Luna from making their children werewolves by making them fundamentally non-human, ie killing them or mutating them into something horrible and alien. Otherwise, if the fundamental tapestry of the human is still there, the Warden Moon can repaint it as desired.<br /> - Luna generally will not give two fucks about whether someone will Awaken or not, and doesn't have that level of... planned control over turning people into Uratha in the first place, or at least not according to a plan that a human could decipher. It's a warden god of vast scope, with one half of its body ever turned towards the black depths of the void and the madness beyond. That said, if somehow Luna decided it was necessary to infect specific people with its flesh-and-mind-warping taint to stop them Awakening, <i>and</i> those people happened to be the children of an Archmage...<br /> - ...Luna wouldn't care in the least about the Pax. The Pax is a nice story the Archmasters tell themselves for comfort. It's far nicer to believe that actually they're all akin to gods who can rewrite the world in their image but only refrain from doing so due to MAD, than the reality which is that they are small, small fish in a very big pond of entities that don't particularly care about them. The Pure are a far bigger threat to Luna than any number of petulant Archmasters upset that they aren't really the secret masters of the world.<br /> <br /> Again, to reiterate, this is the kinda way I use Awakening when running Werewolf. Other game lines should <i>always</i> come second to whatever game line you're running.<br /> <br /> One Chronicle I ran, the Awakened made the horrifying discovery that their myths of 'Atlantis' were due to magic having been taught to humanity by evil, horrible fishmen fomori, whose actual backstory was more strongly related to that of the Uratha and Father Wolf and to whom the creation of the Awakened was a minor and irrelevant side-project.<br /> <br /> When I run Mage, the reverse occurs - Mage comes first, other game lines' settings get wrapped around it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T23:23:12-08:00","id":412485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/409279-mage-transitioning-to-werewolf?p=411270#post411270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno whether vampires can, can't remember if there's any limitation based on having to be alive or whatnot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My own tendency would be to allow it; it certainly gets entertaining when you start bringing vampires in as the targets of some pack rites <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, it's not like Vampires are all friendly to each other, and having a group of raging Uratha at your back when someone tries to teach you a lesson is never wrong!<br /> <br /> I like it for the differences in powers, especially Gangrel vs. Werewolf shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Hmm.. Yeah. I have to do this now. Time to update Blood Tenebrous from 1e rules, it seems...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}